00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:34.570
My father was a drug dealer.

00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:35.817
Engineer, drug dealer.

00:00:35.817 --> 00:00:36.910
(laughs)

00:00:36.910 --> 00:00:38.963
Engineer by day, drug dealer at night.

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:43.100
I saw a lot of crazy things growing up.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:45.000
Things I probably shouldn't have seen.

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:48.463
Abuse. Physical, sexual.

00:00:49.390 --> 00:00:51.590
- [Interviewer] From who?
From stepdad, or dad?

00:00:51.590 --> 00:00:56.120
- No, from uncles. Just physical abuse,

00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:57.623
mental abuse from my mother.

00:00:59.170 --> 00:01:02.377
My father, well, my
stepfather was there a lot.

00:01:02.377 --> 00:01:05.390
Never abused me. Kind of protected me,

00:01:05.390 --> 00:01:08.490
so I love him very much.

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:10.767
He was always a protector.

00:01:10.767 --> 00:01:11.816
- [Interviewer] It's nice
to have somebody lookout.

00:01:11.816 --> 00:01:14.553
- Yeah, he protected me from my mom a lot.

00:01:14.553 --> 00:01:15.386
- [Interviewer] From your mom?

00:01:15.386 --> 00:01:16.386
- Mhm. Yeah.

00:01:17.237 --> 00:01:20.423
- [Interviewer] And the sexual
abuse, what age did it start?

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:22.820
- About...

00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:26.126
four or five.

00:01:26.126 --> 00:01:26.959
- [Interviewer] Really?

00:01:26.959 --> 00:01:27.840
- Mhm.

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:28.860
- [Interviewer] There's
a lot of it or just-

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:31.450
- Yeah, a lot of it.

00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:32.420
Anytime

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:36.993
they would get a chance.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:43.200
My mother wasn't a very vigilant person.

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:46.360
She believed that if you were
like, from the same culture,

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:48.870
you wouldn't hurt someone like that.

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:50.170
She just had real

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:54.380
ignorant beliefs

00:01:55.233 --> 00:01:56.473
and thoughts,

00:01:58.866 --> 00:02:00.516
and never believed a word I said.

00:02:04.263 --> 00:02:06.415
- [Interviewer] What age
were you when you left home?

00:02:06.415 --> 00:02:09.620
- I didn't leave home, my
mother threw me out. I was 13.

00:02:09.620 --> 00:02:10.900
- [Interviewer] Your
mom threw you out at 13?

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:14.634
- In the winter, five
days before Christmas.

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:15.801
- [Interviewer] Five
days before Christmas?

00:02:15.801 --> 00:02:16.634
- Yes.

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:20.430
- [Interviewer] Where
did you go from there?

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:24.483
- I went to go live with a
pimp and his prostitutes,

00:02:25.420 --> 00:02:28.883
and I started selling crack for them.

00:02:30.688 --> 00:02:32.240
- [Interviewer] You weren't
having sex for money?

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:33.073
- No.

00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:36.070
I was always really afraid of men

00:02:36.070 --> 00:02:39.690
because of what happened
to me when I was younger,

00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:41.350
but then I did end up meeting

00:02:42.690 --> 00:02:46.700
someone that ended up abusing me

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:51.587
even more and making me
more unstable than I was,

00:02:52.567 --> 00:02:54.926
Older gentlemen, you know?

00:02:54.926 --> 00:02:58.100
Now I look back on it
and I'm like, a predator.

00:02:58.100 --> 00:02:59.500
He was a predator back then,

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:04.363
and that made my life even more,

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:07.853
my mental states spin out of control.

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:11.983
I did continue going to
school and educate myself,

00:03:14.531 --> 00:03:16.700
and I was never able to really hold down.

00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:17.940
I've gotten great jobs,

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:22.940
never been able to hold a city
job down because of my mind,

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:26.310
just racing thoughts all the time.

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:28.160
Things have happened to me, you know?

00:03:29.190 --> 00:03:34.190
So, I think I was 27 when
I started using heroin.

00:03:34.829 --> 00:03:36.243
I was 27.

00:03:37.203 --> 00:03:40.760
That was the first time the
noise shut off in my head.

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:41.593
- [Interviewer] Shut off the pain?

00:03:41.593 --> 00:03:42.680
- Just shut off.

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:43.600
Pain.

00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:44.433
- [Interviewer] I've heard that a lot.

00:03:44.433 --> 00:03:46.283
- Everything, it just went away.

00:03:47.710 --> 00:03:49.850
It wasn't the most pleasant experience,

00:03:49.850 --> 00:03:52.123
because I threw up and it was just gross,

00:03:53.230 --> 00:03:57.400
but the thought of me not thinking

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:59.770
about things that have
happened to me, the thought

00:03:59.770 --> 00:04:02.980
